   "claim": "Combining time masking with channel masking during pre-training raises sleep-staging AUC from 94.8 (channel masking alone with SimCLR) to 96.7, supporting the claim that channel-invariant feature learning is essential for pre-training (Table 1 ablation).",
   "rationale": "In work/logs/C00080.log the decision line gives mean full-channel AUC time_only 0.735, channel_only 0.905, both 0.897 (3 seeds); the pre-registered rule needs both > channel_only > time_only, and 'both' is 0.008 below channel_only (pooled SD 0.0175, i.e. statistically indistinguishable), so the 'adding time masking raises AUC over channel-only' half is not reproduced on this synthetic data, while the 'channel masking >> time-only' half is (gap +0.170; missing-channel mean AUC 0.577 / 0.703 / 0.692). This speaks only to a synthetic proxy (600-step nano ViT, cross-channel-redundant generator I designed) and not to the real MROS values; the secondary DINO run with the repo's DINOCLSModel (300 steps) stayed near chance (full AUC 0.529-0.537) and carries no weight."
  }
